      "body": "## Motivation\n\ndLLM requests held in `dllm_manager.waiting_queue` between denoising rounds could fall outside `SGLANG_REQ_RUNNING_TIMEOUT` coverage after their first forward.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Include dLLM manager-held requests in running-timeout polling.\n- Preserve existing timeout guards, request ID deduplication, and rank-consistent abort handling.\n- Add a focused regression covering stale, fresh, and never-started manager-held requests, including duplicate membership in a running batch.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nN/A. This does not change model outputs.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A. This is a scheduler timeout correctness fix.\n\nCPU timeout unit tests: 11 passed, 2 subtests passed. The new regression fails before the fix and passes afterward.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Formatted with pre-commit\n- [x] Added unit test coverage\n- [x] Followed SGLang code style\n- [ ] Documentation update not needed\n- [ ] Accuracy/speed benchmarks not applicable\n\nRelated: #39499\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39272823538](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39272823538)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39272823467](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39272823467)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39272823730](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39272823730)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
